@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.1926 = private unnamed_addr constant [1327 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of the `functools.lru_cache` and `functools.cache`\0Adecorators on methods.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AUsing the `functools.lru_cache` and `functools.cache` decorators on methods\0Acan lead to memory leaks, as the global cache will retain a reference to\0Athe instance, preventing it from being garbage collected.\0A\0AInstead, refactor the method to depend only on its arguments and not on the\0Ainstance of the class, or use the `@lru_cache` decorator on a function\0Aoutside of the class.\0A\0AThis rule ignores instance methods on enumeration classes, as enum members\0Aare singletons.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom functools import lru_cache\0A\0A\0Adef square(x: int) -> int:\0A    return x * x\0A\0A\0Aclass Number:\0A    value: int\0A\0A    @lru_cache\0A    def squared(self):\0A        return square(self.value)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom functools import lru_cache\0A\0A\0A@lru_cache\0Adef square(x: int) -> int:\0A    return x * x\0A\0A\0Aclass Number:\0A    value: int\0A\0A    def squared(self):\0A        return square(self.value)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `functools.lru_cache`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functools.html#functools.lru_cache)\0A- [Python documentation: `functools.cache`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functools.html#functools.cache)\0A- [don't lru_cache methods!](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sVjtp6tGo0g)\0A", align 1
