@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2006 = private unnamed_addr constant [987 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for typed function arguments in stubs with complex default values.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AStub (`.pyi`) files exist as \22data files\22 for static analysis tools, and\0Aare not evaluated at runtime. While simple default values may be useful for\0Asome tools that consume stubs, such as IDEs, they are ignored by type\0Acheckers.\0A\0AInstead of including and reproducing a complex value, use `...` to indicate\0Athat the assignment has a default value, but that the value is \22complex\22 or\0Avaries according to the current platform or Python version. For the\0Apurposes of this rule, any default value counts as \22complex\22 unless it is\0Aa literal `int`, `float`, `complex`, `bytes`, `str`, `bool`, `None`, `...`,\0Aor a simple container literal.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```pyi\0Adef foo(arg: list[int] = list(range(10_000))) -> None: ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```pyi\0Adef foo(arg: list[int] = ...) -> None: ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [`flake8-pyi`](https://github.com/PyCQA/flake8-pyi/blob/main/ERRORCODES.md)\0A", align 1
@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2007 = private unnamed_addr constant [54 x i8] c"Only simple default values allowed for typed arguments", align 1
