@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2083 = private unnamed_addr constant [1272 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for unnecessary `request.addfinalizer` usages in `pytest` fixtures.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`pytest` offers two ways to perform cleanup in fixture code. The first is\0Asequential (via the `yield` statement), the second callback-based (via\0A`request.addfinalizer`).\0A\0AThe sequential approach is more readable and should be preferred, unless\0Athe fixture uses the \22factory as fixture\22 pattern.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0A@pytest.fixture()\0Adef my_fixture(request):\0A    resource = acquire_resource()\0A    request.addfinalizer(resource.release)\0A    return resource\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0A@pytest.fixture()\0Adef my_fixture():\0A    resource = acquire_resource()\0A    yield resource\0A    resource.release()\0A\0A\0A# \22factory-as-fixture\22 pattern\0A@pytest.fixture()\0Adef my_factory(request):\0A    def create_resource(arg):\0A        resource = acquire_resource(arg)\0A        request.addfinalizer(resource.release)\0A        return resource\0A\0A    return create_resource\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [`pytest` documentation: Adding finalizers directly](https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/how-to/fixtures.html#adding-finalizers-directly)\0A- [`pytest` documentation: Factories as fixtures](https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/how-to/fixtures.html#factories-as-fixtures)\0A", align 1
