@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2086 = private unnamed_addr constant [848 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for unnecessary `yield` expressions in `pytest` fixtures.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIn `pytest` fixtures, the `yield` expression should only be used for fixtures\0Athat include teardown code, to clean up the fixture after the test function\0Ahas finished executing.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0A@pytest.fixture()\0Adef my_fixture():\0A    resource = acquire_resource()\0A    yield resource\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0A@pytest.fixture()\0Adef my_fixture_with_teardown():\0A    resource = acquire_resource()\0A    yield resource\0A    resource.release()\0A\0A\0A@pytest.fixture()\0Adef my_fixture_without_teardown():\0A    resource = acquire_resource()\0A    return resource\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [`pytest` documentation: Teardown/Cleanup](https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/how-to/fixtures.html#teardown-cleanup-aka-fixture-finalization)\0A", align 1
