@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2098 = private unnamed_addr constant [1290 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the type of parameter names passed to `pytest.mark.parametrize`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `argnames` argument of `pytest.mark.parametrize` takes a string or\0Aa sequence of strings. For a single parameter, it's preferable to use a\0Astring. For multiple parameters, it's preferable to use the style\0Aconfigured via the [`lint.flake8-pytest-style.parametrize-names-type`] setting.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0A# single parameter, always expecting string\0A@pytest.mark.parametrize((\22param\22,), [1, 2, 3])\0Adef test_foo(param): ...\0A\0A\0A# multiple parameters, expecting tuple\0A@pytest.mark.parametrize([\22param1\22, \22param2\22], [(1, 2), (3, 4)])\0Adef test_bar(param1, param2): ...\0A\0A\0A# multiple parameters, expecting tuple\0A@pytest.mark.parametrize(\22param1,param2\22, [(1, 2), (3, 4)])\0Adef test_baz(param1, param2): ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0A@pytest.mark.parametrize(\22param\22, [1, 2, 3])\0Adef test_foo(param): ...\0A\0A\0A@pytest.mark.parametrize((\22param1\22, \22param2\22), [(1, 2), (3, 4)])\0Adef test_bar(param1, param2): ...\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-pytest-style.parametrize-names-type`\0A\0A## References\0A- [`pytest` documentation: How to parametrize fixtures and test functions](https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/how-to/parametrize.html#pytest-mark-parametrize)\0A", align 1
