@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2120 = private unnamed_addr constant [551 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the presence of a `return None` statement when `None` is the only\0Apossible return value.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0APython implicitly assumes `return None` if an explicit `return` value is\0Aomitted. Therefore, explicitly returning `None` is redundant and should be\0Aavoided when it is the only possible `return` value across all code paths\0Ain a given function.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef foo(bar):\0A    if not bar:\0A        return\0A    return None\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef foo(bar):\0A    if not bar:\0A        return\0A    return\0A```\0A", align 1
