@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2146 = private unnamed_addr constant [572 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `else` statements with a `continue` statement in the preceding\0A`if` block.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `else` statement is not needed, as the `continue` statement will always\0Acontinue onto the next iteration of a loop. Removing the `else` will reduce\0Anesting and make the code more readable.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef foo(bar, baz):\0A    for i in bar:\0A        if i < baz:\0A            continue\0A        else:\0A            x = 0\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef foo(bar, baz):\0A    for i in bar:\0A        if i < baz:\0A            continue\0A        x = 0\0A```\0A", align 1
